      "raw": "After analyzing all three views, we observe that each view contains three garments: a white button-up shirt, a black satin skirt with lace trim, and a black long-sleeve top (possibly a turtleneck or high-neck blouse). The garments are shown in different arrangements across the views, but their visual characteristics (fabric, color, construction) remain consistent.\n\nIn each view, the available regions (R001\u2013R003, R004\u2013R006, R007\u2013R009) correspond to these three garments, and each region is a crop of one of the garments. The regions are labeled consistently across views, and the garments are visually distinct and identifiable by their unique features:\n\n- **White shirt**: Light-colored, button-up, with a collar and visible buttons. Appears in R001, R004, R007.\n- **Black satin skirt with lace trim**: Shiny black fabric with a scalloped lace hem. Appears in R002, R005, R008.\n- **Black long-sleeve top**: Solid black, long-sleeved, high-neck or turtleneck style. Appears in R003, R006, R009.\n\nEach garment is visible in every view, and the regions for each garment are consistent across views (same garment, same region ID pattern). There is no mixing of garments in any mask, and each region corresponds to a single, distinct garment.\n\nThus, we can form three tracks, one for each garment, using the region IDs from each view.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tracks\": [\n    {\n      \"garment\": \"white button-up shirt with collar and buttons\",\n      \"regions\": [\"R001\", \"R004\", \"R007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"garment\": \"black satin skirt with lace trim\",\n      \"regions\": [\"R002\", \"R005\", \"R008\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"garment\": \"black long-sleeve high-neck top\",\n      \"regions\": [\"R003\", \"R006\", \"R009\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```",
